(Most of the adventures recorded in this book really occurred; one or two) Tj
T*
(were experiences of my own, the rest those of boys who were schoolmates) Tj
T*
(of mine. Huck Finn is drawn from life; Tom Sawyer also, but not from an) Tj
T*
(individual-he is a combination of the characteristics of three boys whom) Tj
T*
(I knew, and therefore belongs to the composite order of architecture.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The odd superstitions touched upon were all prevalent among children and) Tj
T*
(slaves in the West at the period of this story-that is to say, thirty or) Tj
T*
(forty years ago.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Although my book is intended mainly for the entertainment of boys and) Tj
T*
(girls, I hope it will not be shunned by men and women on that account,) Tj
T*
(for part of my plan has been to try to pleasantly remind adults of what) Tj
T*
(they once were themselves, and of how they felt and thought and talked,) Tj
T*
(and what queer enterprises they sometimes engaged in.) Tj
